      "problem": "$3{tan}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The angles ${30}^{∘}$ and ${45}^{∘}$ are special, and their trigonometric ratios have the  values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}=1.\n$$\n\nAlso, note that ${tan}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}$ simply means $(\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘})^{2}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{tan}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘} & = \\\\ 3{(\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘})}^{2}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘} & = \\\\ 3{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})}^{2}-1 & = \\\\ 3(\\frac{3}{9})-1 & = \\\\ 1-1 & = \\\\ 0 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
